nx2: mark GPU-written pages 64 at a time

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone.

Source: zortos293/Lichii PR 178 (tibzejoker), head 95a227b710, GPL-3.0-or-later. Only this part:
PR 178's UsageTracker part touches the lines of lichii-cpu-0235, which does the same job from PR 184.

Storage buffer binds mark megabytes as written, almost all marked already: one load per 64 pages
instead of one per page. Runs on the back thread. Lichii numbers are from an RTX 4090 and an i9, so
none is given.

Runs on the PS5: yes, every written storage buffer bind. No switch: the bits end up the same.
Hang: cannot add one. Pool memory: none.
Checked: 2 million random marks on the Mac, bit arrays equal to the old loop's.

diff --git a/src/video_core/nx2.h b/src/video_core/nx2.h
index 92714d52d2..7f1c90b388 100644
--- a/src/video_core/nx2.h
+++ b/src/video_core/nx2.h
@@ -34,12 +34,16 @@ inline void Nx2MarkGpuWritten(u64 device_address, u64 size) {
     }
     const u64 last = std::min<u64>((device_address + size - 1) >> Nx2WrittenPageBits,
                                    g_nx2_gpu_written_pages.size() * 64 - 1);
-    for (u64 page = device_address >> Nx2WrittenPageBits; page <= last; ++page) {
+    // A word at a time (Lichii PR 178): storage buffer binds mark megabytes, mostly marked already.
+    for (u64 page = device_address >> Nx2WrittenPageBits; page <= last;) {
+        const u64 first_bit = page % 64;
+        const u64 bits = std::min<u64>(64 - first_bit, last - page + 1);
+        const u64 mask = (bits == 64 ? ~u64{0} : (u64{1} << bits) - 1) << first_bit;
         auto& word = g_nx2_gpu_written_pages[page / 64];
-        const u64 bit = u64{1} << (page % 64);
-        if ((word.load(std::memory_order_relaxed) & bit) == 0) {
-            word.fetch_or(bit, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        if ((word.load(std::memory_order_relaxed) & mask) != mask) {
+            word.fetch_or(mask, std::memory_order_relaxed);
         }
+        page += bits;
     }
 }
 
